Process and Service Management
===============================================================
Goal: Find top 5 CPU processes, find zombie processes, check which
process uses port 80, reload httpd with SIGHUP, renice httpd to 10,
and verify the nice value.


STEP 0 (only if httpd is not running): Start httpd
--------------------------------------------------
$ sudo systemctl start httpd
$ sudo systemctl status httpd


STEP 1: Display top 5 processes sorted by CPU using ps
------------------------------------------------------
$ ps aux --sort=-%cpu | head -n 6

(head -n 6 = 1 header line + 5 processes)


STEP 2: Find any zombie processes
---------------------------------
$ top -b -n 1 | grep "zombie"

Expected output (no zombies):
Tasks: 238 total, 1 running, 237 sleeping, 0 stopped, 0 zombie

Alternative using ps (zombies show state Z):
$ ps aux | awk '$8 ~ /^Z/'


STEP 3: Identify which process is using port 80 using ss
--------------------------------------------------------
$ sudo ss -tulpn | grep ':80'

Output shows httpd with its PIDs listening on *:80


STEP 4: Send SIGHUP to httpd (graceful reload, no downtime)
-----------------------------------------------------------
Find the PIDs:
$ pgrep -x httpd

Find the main (oldest) httpd PID:
$ pgrep -o httpd

Send SIGHUP to the main process (replace <PID> with that number):
$ sudo kill -HUP <PID>

Or by name:
$ sudo pkill -HUP -x httpd

Or the service way:
$ sudo systemctl reload httpd

NOTE: Do NOT use kill -9. That is SIGKILL, it stops httpd
instantly and is not a graceful reload. (If you used it, start
httpd again with: sudo systemctl start httpd)


STEP 5: Find the httpd main PID and renice it to 10
---------------------------------------------------
$ pgrep -o httpd
$ sudo renice -n 10 -p <PID>

Example output:
34463 (process ID) old priority 0, new priority 10


STEP 6: Verify the nice value changed using ps
----------------------------------------------
$ ps -o ni -p <PID>

Expected output:
 NI
 10

Or see name too:
$ ps -o pid,ni,comm -p <PID>


QUICK COMMAND SUMMARY
---------------------
ps aux --sort=-%cpu | head -n 6    -> top 5 CPU processes
top -b -n 1 | grep "zombie"        -> zombie count
sudo ss -tulpn | grep ':80'        -> who is using port 80
pgrep -o httpd                     -> main httpd PID
sudo kill -HUP <PID>               -> graceful reload
sudo renice -n 10 -p <PID>         -> set nice value to 10
ps -o ni -p <PID>                  -> verify nice valuePRACTICAL P-06: Process and Service Management
